  "result": "Perfect! I've successfully implemented customer statements. Here's a summary:\n\n## Summary of Changes\n\n**New Module: `src/statements.js`**\n\nCreated `statement(customerId, invoices, asOf)` function that:\n- Normalizes and validates the customer ID (returns `CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND` if invalid)\n- Filters invoices by:\n  - **Customer match**: only invoices for the specified customer\n  - **Status**: only 'issued' or 'partially_paid' (excludes draft and paid)\n  - **Date**: only invoices with issueDate on or before asOf\n- Sorts filtered invoices by issueDate (ascending)\n- Returns each invoice with:\n  - `number`: invoice number\n  - `issueDate`: date invoice was issued\n  - `dueDate`: payment due date\n  - `total`: invoice total (from invoiceTotals)\n  - `due`: amount still owed (from balanceDue)\n- Calculates `totalDue` as the sum of all due amounts\n- Returns structure: `ok({ customerId, invoices, totalDue })`\n\n**Test Coverage: 19 comprehensive tests**\n- Empty statement for customer with no invoices\n- Customer validation and ID normalization\n- Invoice filtering by status (issued, partially_paid, draft, paid)\n- Invoice filtering by date (before/on/after asOf)\n- Sorting by issueDate\n- Correct invoice field structure\n- Due calculation with partial payments\n- Total due aggregation\n- Multiple invoices with discounts, VAT, and payments\n- Customer isolation (filtering correct customer from mixed list)\n- Year boundary date handling\n\n**Test Results**: All 203 tests pass (184 previous + 19 new statement tests)",
